# `DESC` in caps is DS0105, and the key still sorts descending (M1-19).
mode: syntax
---- query
T | sort by a DESC
---- expected
PROGRAM@0..19
  PIPELINE@0..18
    NAME_REF@0..1
      IDENT@0..1 "T"
    WHITESPACE@1..2 " "
    PIPE@2..3 "|"
    WHITESPACE@3..4 " "
    SORT_OP@4..18
      IDENT@4..8 "sort"
      WHITESPACE@8..9 " "
      IDENT@9..11 "by"
      WHITESPACE@11..12 " "
      SORT_KEY@12..18
        NAME_REF@12..13
          IDENT@12..13 "a"
        WHITESPACE@13..14 " "
        IDENT@14..18 "DESC"
  WHITESPACE@18..19 "\n"

error[DS0105]: SQL keyword `DESC` is not a sort direction
  --> query:1:15
  |
1 | T | sort by a DESC
  |               ^^^^
  |
  = help: keywords are lowercase: write `desc`

with the machine-applicable fixes applied:
    T | sort by a desc
which parses without errors
